 about this place is that I found out about it the day before I went home. This is a cute little place right by Bar Tonique on Rampart. The set up is pretty standard cafe kind of vibe; art work on the walls and very clean. They bake everything fresh and the food you get is fresh and delicious, no fried badness! This is a big deal to me when I have been on a 5 day bender of tater tots and beer. My friend took me here for some lunch before the easter parades and I ordered an iced coffee and a turkey wrap - SO GOOD. I think they make their own Mayonnaise. That or they managed to make the stuff from a jar taste fabulous. Fabulous. Yes that is my word for this place. Give it a w..."},{"business_id":"pbAfraRFRDsyvSB856dryg","review_id":"W8yem5CmE0rXXsK9eKc1lQ","date":"2010-11-05T14:29:21","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.8992834091186523,"text_excerpt":"A...MAZ...ING place. I recently moved to NO from Boston and have been in search of a cool cafe..not overly touristy, great fresh coffee, great, fresh food and a cool, laidback vibe. Decadence cafe is IT! Great food (breakfast and lunch), great prices, great owners. Dog-friendly. The breakfast biscuits make you wonder why you ever slummed at McDonald's."}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
